WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.576
Raj: Connection checkout time is normal again. Each worker has available connections now.

2
00:00:06.576 --> 00:00:13.007
Hannah: What about checked-out connections over time? A fresh pool can hide leakage.

3
00:00:13.007 --> 00:00:19.151
Anika: They're stable under the reduced traffic. That doesn't prove cancellation is fixed.

4
00:00:19.151 --> 00:00:26.182
Priya: Just to confirm, reports stay paused, right? Don't remove both safeguards together.

5
00:00:26.182 --> 00:00:31.990
Lukas: Agreed. We're back to baseline now. State the limits with that update.

6
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:38.518
Raj: If the pool is exhausted again, stop. Maybe another path holds connections too.

7
00:00:38.518 --> 00:00:45.333
Hannah: Let's keep it under observation tonight. Track connection age beside checkout waits.

8
00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:52.245
Anika: Okay, isolated testing is running now. The first cancelled request retained ownership.

9
00:00:52.245 --> 00:00:58.484
Lukas: Repeat it against the current release. One sample isn't the complete diagnosis.

10
00:00:58.484 --> 00:01:04.820
Priya: So, keep recovery and repair separate. We'll review that test evidence next.

